# the sounds, as a hand has them: SEL + KNOB 1 on Keys, Melody and Bass, SEL + KNOB 2 on Keys for the pad; the knobs as ever otherwise, here and on the other pages; Degrees and the SEL + button combinations stay what they are; in Hands and in Auto; each piece keeps its own; a save keeps them, range-checked; an older save is not read; MIDI and the rest: tests/host/sound_test.c
wait 300
expect unfit 0
expect par28 0
expect par29 0
expect par30 0
expect par31 0
expect enagree 0
listen
# ---- the header says the sound
tap ENV
wait 300
said Keys page: Level 60, Bloom 50, Bright 50, Notes 3. Sound Electric, pad sound Warm
shot keys_page.png
# ---- SEL + KNOB 1: the keys' sound, a detent at a time, round. The knob's value does not move, no Degrees come
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par28 1
expect par4 60
said KEYS SOUND Clear
wait 400
expect screen 2
spin K1 1
expect par28 2
said KEYS SOUND Organ
spin K1 1
expect par28 3
said KEYS SOUND Felt
spin K1 1
expect par28 0
said KEYS SOUND Electric
spin K1 -1
expect par28 3
wait 600
expect enagree 0
shot keys_felt.png
wait 1000
shot keys_header.png
release SEL
wait 100
expect view 1
expect mutekeys 0
expect screen 2
# ---- SEL + KNOB 2: the pad's. The keys' stays
press SEL
spin K2 1
expect par29 1
expect par28 3
expect par5 50
said PAD SOUND Airy
release SEL
wait 100
# ---- KNOB 3 and 4 with SEL on Keys, and all of them without it: what they ever were
press SEL
spin K3 1
expect par6 51
expect par28 3
spin K3 -1
release SEL
spin K1 1
expect par4 61
expect par28 3
spin K1 -1
spin K2 1
expect par5 51
expect par29 1
spin K2 -1
# ---- SEL on other pages: as ever: a knob is its value. Home
tap HOME
wait 100
press SEL
spin K2 1
expect par1 71
spin K2 -1
release SEL
tap SEQ
wait 100
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par16 46
spin K1 -1
release SEL
# ---- SEL alone still shows the Degrees, and SEL + a turn goes back to the page and it stays there this hold; the next hold has them again
tap LFO
wait 300
said Bass page: Level 50, Move 50, Glide 10, Octave 0. Sound Warm
press SEL
wait 400
expect screen 8
spin K1 1
expect par30 1
said BASS SOUND Sub
wait 300
expect screen 2
wait 300
expect screen 2
release SEL
wait 100
press SEL
wait 400
expect screen 8
release SEL
wait 100
expect screen 2
expect view 3
# SEL + a button, SEL + a key after a turn in the same hold: they still are what they are
expect mutebass 1
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par30 2
said BASS SOUND Hollow
tap LFO
wait 50
expect mutebass 0
tap LFO
wait 50
expect mutebass 1
release SEL
expect view 3
# ---- the melody: Auto, then the timbres
tap ARP
wait 300
said Melody page: Level 60, Rate 50, Tone 50, Octave 0. Sound Auto
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par31 1
said MELODY SOUND Flute
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par31 5
said MELODY SOUND Music box
wait 600
shot melody_box.png
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par31 0
said MELODY SOUND Auto
spin K1 -1
spin K1 -1
expect par31 5
release SEL
# ---- the MIDI says nothing of it: the same channels and notes go on (the whole of it: sound_test). A help card still comes, and says so
press ARP
wait 1000
expect help 9
said SEL + KNOB 1: THE SOUND
release ARP
wait 100
expect view 2
# ---- it does the same in Auto
press SEL
tap HOME
release SEL
wait 100
expect mode 0
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par31 6
release SEL
wait 100
expect enagree 0
expect dirty 1
press SEL
tap HOME
release SEL
wait 100
expect mode 1
# ---- each piece keeps its own. A quick turn: the last piece, all of it, within the queue's guarantee
turn PRESET 1 1
wait 100
expect piece 1
expect par28 0
expect par31 0
expect enagree 0
tap LFO
press SEL
spin K1 1
expect par30 1
release SEL
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 30
expect piece 4
expect par30 0
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -4 1
wait 30
expect piece 0
expect par28 3
expect par29 1
expect par30 2
expect par31 6
expect enagree 0
flood 200
turn PRESET 1 1
turn PRESET -1 1
wait 60
expect enagree 0
expect par28 3
# ---- SAVE held: the piece back to its recipe, the first sounds
press SAVE
wait 1600
release SAVE
wait 100
expect par28 0
expect par29 0
expect par30 0
expect par31 0
expect enagree 0
# ---- what is chosen survives the power going off, for the piece playing and another
tap ENV
press SEL
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 1
release SEL
tap LFO
press SEL
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
release SEL
tap ARP
press SEL
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
release SEL
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 100
tap LFO
press SEL
spin K1 1
release SEL
wait 100
expect par30 1
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 100
tap SAVE
wait 800
reboot
wait 300
expect piece 0
expect par28 2
expect par29 3
expect par30 3
expect par31 4
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 100
expect par30 1
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 100
expect par28 2
# ---- a sound out of range in a save: it is damaged, the recipes. Each of them, on the piece playing and on a piece not playing
storebad -1 28 4
reboot
wait 300
expect par28 0
expect enagree 0
storebad 3 29 -1
reboot
wait 300
expect par29 0
storebad 5 30 4
reboot
wait 300
expect par30 0
storebad 7 31 7
reboot
wait 300
expect par31 0
expect enagree 0
# and in range is read, up to the last
tap ENV
press SEL
spin K1 1
release SEL
wait 100
storebad 7 31 6
reboot
wait 300
expect par28 1
turn PRESET -1 1
wait 100
expect piece 7
expect par31 6
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET 1 1
wait 100
# ---- an older save: refused, whether its format or its length says so, and it falls back to the recipes
tap ENV
press SEL
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
release SEL
wait 100
expect par28 3
storeold
reboot
wait 300
expect par28 0
expect par4 60
expect enagree 0
press SEL
spin K1 1
release SEL
expect par28 0
press SEL
tap HOME
release SEL
wait 100
expect arrange 0
storeshort
reboot
wait 300
expect arrange 1
expect par28 0
expect enagree 0
